# Jev API key (TypeSafe System One). Grading uses this key.
# 1. Create a key at https://console.typesafe.ai/keys
# 2. Copy this file to .env
# 3. Paste the key as VITE_JEV_API_KEY
# 4. Restart `npm run dev`
#
# The browser cannot call api.typesafe.ai (the API rejects browser origins),
# so the Vite dev server and the Netlify function read this value and proxy
# POST /api/jev. Client code never reads the key, so Vite does not bundle it.
# On Netlify you can set VITE_JEV_API_KEY or JEV_API_KEY in the site environment.
# Never commit .env or a real key.
VITE_JEV_API_KEY=

# Gemini API key. Sample practice questions use this. Follow-up coach chat
# uses it when it is set; otherwise the coach answers from the Jev grades.
# 1. Create a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# 2. Paste the key as VITE_API_KEY
# 3. Restart `npm run dev`
VITE_API_KEY=

# Optional. Set to true to preview critique and chat without calling Jev or Gemini.
# Leave this unset when the keys above are real. If mock mode is set, it wins.
# VITE_MOCK_GEMINI=true
